faqs:
  - q: "How does the business day calculation filter weekends?"
    a: "When you check the business days option, the calculator skips Saturdays and Sundays during iteration. If adding 5 business days starting on a Friday, the tool advances through Monday to Friday, producing the exact working day target."
  - q: "How are leap years handled when adding years or months?"
    a: "The tool accounts for leap year structures automatically. Adding 365 calendar days across a leap year appropriately factors in February 29th, ensuring exact calendar alignment without manual correction."
  - q: "Can I calculate dates in the past by subtracting days?"
    a: "Yes, simply select Subtract from the operation dropdown menu. You can count backward by days, weeks, months, or years to determine exact historical dates for contract origin, notice periods, or historical research."
  - q: "What happens if I add a month to January 31st?"
    a: "Standard calendar math adjusts month-end overflows to the last valid day of the target month. For example, adding one month to January 31st lands on February 28th (or February 29th during leap years)."
  - q: "Is any of my date input data stored on external servers?"
